  "problem": "The average distance from the origin to a point on the circumference of the circle is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .",
  "worked_solution": "Since $r(\\theta )$ represents the distance of each point on the circle from the origin, the average distance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{[\\frac{\\pi }{2}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})]}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}6\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }(6\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta ){|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }(6\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-6\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }(6-(-6)) \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
